  "product": "clk_cod_ops",
  "design": "Combines the screening signature (co-located differential cancels common-mode, reveals M2) with the gravitational identification (M2 phase matches cos(2*(lon1-lon2))). For each remote station j, the cross-spectrum between the differential and station j's clock has a phase at M2. If this phase matches the gravitational prediction, the differential signal is gravitational. This requires ALL THREE properties simultaneously: (1) differential has M2 power (screening), (2) M2 phase matches gravitational prediction (identification), (3) phase is coherent across remote stations at different longitudes (replication).",
  "prediction": "TEP: M2 r > 0 and significantly exceeds control r. S2 r > 0 but weaker than M2 (atmospheric phase scatter). Control r ~ 0. M2 r_differential > M2 r_atomic (screening: differential reveals what atomic clock alone cannot see).",
